00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:03.590
JOE: Different environments and
different situations can cause

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:08.410
individuals with sensory problems to
suffer sensory overload, and this has

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:12.290
to be considered when architects and
designers are creating spaces as they

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.669
need to factor this into their designs.

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:18.790
Small changes to an environment can
make changes to how an individual

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.810
with autism responds to stimuli.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.110
However, all environments cannot be
made suitable for the sensory needs

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.660
of all individuals with autism.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.500
BETH: There are things that can be done
in the home, schools and workplaces and

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.999
public buildings that can help, such as
changing the environment by addressing

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.270
any possible causes of over stimulation
which may cause sensory overload.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.660
The most important thing is to be aware
of the sensory stimuli that the individual

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.720
responds to and how it affects them.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.280
Sometimes preparing an individual
for some form of potential stimuli

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:53.559
can help them to be prepared.

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:56.960
JOE: In the home, making sure that
lights are not too bright and don’t

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.370
flicker, and sounds of electrical goods
are minimalised can relieve problems.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.459
Sunglasses could help to combat
bright lights and blackout curtains

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.720
could help with sleeping and
hiding visual distractions from

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.910
view can improve a workspace.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.380
An oversensitivity to sound can
be helped by shutting doors and

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.160
windows and eliminating unnecessary
sound such as mechanical noise.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:25.439
The problem of everyday smells in the home
can be solved using low odour products.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.129
Individuals who find textures or
patterns of clothing or soft furnishings

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.210
intolerable, can be helped by making sure
that patterns are kept to a minimum and

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:39.600
cushion covers, and other soft furnishings
and clothes have acceptable textures.

00:01:40.139 --> 00:01:44.220
BETH: Each individual with autism
has their own sensory issues and if

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.120
these can be addressed and alleviated
to some extent, they can make a

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.920
world of difference to their lives.

